From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilwojcik93 <adminit@adar.pl>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:06:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtual display: hand the posture size to the driver and
 recreate on resume

Connect the policy to the display backends:

- before a display is created (launch path and recovery path) the wanted size
  is published under the display GUID; the bundled virtual display driver gets
  it as physical_width_mm/physical_height_mm, and the applied size is recorded
  once the driver accepted the new display. SudoVDA has a static EDID and no
  size field, so it logs a warning and keeps its fixed size;
- a resume whose posture crosses the touch size boundary (for example tablet to
  laptop when a keyboard is attached) recreates the client's display before
  streaming resumes. Shared displays are never recreated for one client, and
  an unknown history keeps the display. A reclaimed display that was created on
  the other side of the boundary is replaced, with the outer retry kept alive
  so the session does not fall back to a physical display;
- removing displays forgets their recorded sizes.

The startup/reconnect production test gets a sixth scenario for the crossing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
